   "id": 632966,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"4\">\n  <li>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit.     <table class=\"unnumbered\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"x_1\">x_1</span></th>\n          <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"y_1\">y_1</span></th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>0.3</td>\n          <td>25</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>0.6</td>\n          <td>36</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>1.2</td>\n          <td>45</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>1.8</td>\n          <td>33</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>2.3</td>\n          <td>12</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n<p>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1225887,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = -35.78x^2+ 45.21x + 3.74\">y = -35.78x^2+ 45.21x + 3.74</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1225888,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = -3.72x^2 + 7.34x + 8.67\">y = -3.72x^2 + 7.34x + 8.67</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1225889,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = -30.84x^2+ 49.61x + 8.99\">y = -30.84x^2+ 49.61x + 8.99</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1225890,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\">y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64</span>"
    }
